This is a core work package. Start only after the named providers publish verified native/backend/persistence contracts and the package's implementation scope is authorized. Do not wait for an entire former numbered stage unless that contract acceptance is explicitly listed above. Do not use an unfinished sibling or mocked replacement as a hidden prerequisite.

## Delivered boundary

Selected city/route/place packs, search/bookmarks, bounded query deltas and measured long-duration offline navigation.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Map source adapters, place index and package content; shared loader/subscription changes serialized with their owners.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 06.T01

- [ ] **06.T01.** Extend [stage 05](../contracts/Scale-navigation-and-hosting-contracts.lingua)'s shared map/archive provider, source/coverage and residency path to selected real city data and a larger offline profile. Keep default coarse Earth available and elevation, imagery, routes, supplied 3D models and authored places separate. Add declared elevation/building/3D source adapters that preserve supported height/geometry and report losses; do not route required shape data through the current basemap normalization that drops buildings. Preserve flat ground/footprints where geometry is absent; no procedural relief or building extrusion is inferred from a place name.

### Task 06.T02

- [ ] **06.T02.** Extend region/layer budgets, cost preview, offline pins, partial coverage and progress/cancel/resume. Online on-demand fetching is allowed only through configured sources and budgets; explicit offline mode prevents new network work. Include styles/labels/transforms/available shape data required by the chosen package. Reuse [stage 05](../contracts/Scale-navigation-and-hosting-contracts.lingua)'s loader/query/demand implementation instead of a second map cache/runtime.

### Task 06.T03

- [ ] **06.T03.** Implement paged spatial/semantic indexes, coarse-parent fallback, permitted dedupe and bounded decode/upload/request queues. Add local place search/bookmarks and saved-route inspection; route solving remains a separately tested subset when selected.

### Task 06.T04

- [ ] **06.T04.** Reuse the E4 coherent query/projection cache and I6 demand leases for the selected map/table subset: initial snapshot, atomic revision deltas, overlap/refcounts, grant changes and reconnect/resnapshot. Prove B19 before widening predicates; do not introduce another general database or per-feature polling loop.

### Task 06.T06

- [ ] **06.T06.** Prove 30-minute navigation under the default working-set cap, rapid request cancellation, offline closure, missing-tile fallback, disk-full behavior and resource release. Do not claim building/terrain detail from current normalized basemap tiles.

